<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Ticket 61823826: the missing half of the mic permission fix (8b13ec2b
       made the request FIRE; the hardened runtime was silently denying it).
       Notarization requires signing with the runtime option (hardened
       runtime), and under the hardened runtime microphone capture
       additionally requires this entitlement: without it
       AVAudioApplication.requestRecordPermission (macOS 14+) and
       AVCaptureDevice.requestAccess(for: .audio) return granted=false
       IMMEDIATELY, with no TCC consent dialog, no entry under System
       Settings, Privacy and Security, Microphone, and tccutil reset is a
       no-op because no TCC record ever exists. That is exactly the AUTO_DENY
       the owner reproduced on both Macs (the in-app Microphone Needed alert
       fires, proof the request ran, while the TCC prompt never appears).
       Differential: Accessibility, Screen Recording and Full Disk Access are
       pure-TCC permissions and their prompts DID appear; microphone is the
       only one of the set that is also entitlement-gated, and the only one
       that never prompts. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
